Gift

Gift=T(A,B,x)

No reciprocal obligation.

gift = transfer(x, A, B)

Invariant: value moves without required exchange.

⸻

Barter

T(A,B,x)+T(B,A,y)

barter = swap(A, cow, B, grain)

Invariant: reciprocal transfer without requiring money.

⸻

Sale

asset\rightarrow buyer
money\rightarrow seller

sale = swap(seller, asset, buyer, price)

Money is basically just one operand of SWAP.

