4. Credit/debt family

Loan

transfer(cash, lender, borrower)
repeat(
    transfer(payment, borrower, lender),
    schedule
)

Mathematically:

P_0=\sum_{t=1}^{n}
\frac{Payment_t}{(1+r)^t}

The essential operator is:

value now ↔ value later.

A loan specifically advances funds with expected repayment, generally under agreed interest/time terms. 

⸻

Secured loan

loan(...)
+ collateralize(asset)

⸻

Mortgage

mortgage =
    loan()
    + collateralize(real_property)
    + amortize()

So a mortgage isn’t a totally new creature.

It’s a composition.

⸻

Bond

bond =
    loan()
    + standardized_claim()
    + transferable()

⸻

5. Temporary-access family

Lease

lease =
    grant_right("possess/use", asset)
    + repeat(rent)
    + expiry(T)

Ownership stays with the lessor while possession/use temporarily moves to the lessee. 

⸻

License

license =
    grant_right(
        action="use",
        scope=defined_scope
    )

Important distinction:

ownership stays put; permission moves.

⸻

Subscription

subscription =
    repeat(payment)
    + repeat(grant_access())

Netflix is basically a recursive license.

⸻

Membership

membership =
    subscription()
    + identity()
    + group_rights()

That little addition—identity—changes the behavioral system considerably.

⸻

