8. Authority/custody family

Agency

agency =
    delegate(authority)
    + constrain(scope)
    + fiduciary_invariant()

The important abstraction is:

another actor can legally/socially act as an extension of me.

⸻

Trust

This one is beautiful computationally because it deliberately separates normally bundled variables:

ownership/control → trustee
benefit           → beneficiary
source/instructions → settlor

So:

trust =
    separate(control, benefit)
    + delegate(control, trustee)
    + preserve(beneficiary_interest)

It is an unbundling operator.

⸻

Escrow

Similarly separates:

ownership / possession / release authority.

That’s why these legal structures are useful to Pantheon: law discovered ways of factorizing concepts humans normally lump together.

