9. Risk family

Insurance

Premium_i\rightarrow Pool

and upon covered event:

Loss_i\Rightarrow Payout_i

insurance =
    pool(premiums)
    + condition(loss_event)
    + indemnify(loss)

Insurance is fundamentally a risk-allocation system across many participants. 

⸻

Indemnity

if covered_loss(A):
    B.compensate(A)

Payout=f(Loss)

Indemnity is narrower conceptually:

If this kind of loss happens, I make you whole according to our rule. 

⸻

Guarantee

if debtor.default:
    guarantor.perform()

The guarantor is a fallback source after failure/default. 

⸻

Surety

A related but different structure:

principal.must_perform()
surety.backstops(principal)

Cornell distinguishes a surety’s direct liability from a guarantor whose obligation is triggered by the debtor’s failure. 

So we have:

insurance = distribute risk
indemnity = reimburse loss
guarantee = substitute performer after default
collateral = attach recoverable property

Four different risk operators.

